// Config for the J8 fixture-site Worker (0509#4046). It is a separate Worker
// with its own name and routes block, same shape as the J1 mail sink in
// workers/e2e-inbox.wrangler.jsonc. It lives on fixture.0509.in and NEVER on
// 0509.in: 0509.in is a live production 308 redirect to 0509.io (a zone-level
// Redirect Rule on the 0509.in zone), and a deliberate break there would break
// production. docs/REBUILD-DONE.md J8 says this outright, and
// docs/engines/delivery.md P7.5 requires the incident round-trip to run against
// this fixture and no other host.
//
// The KV namespace id is pinned. The id-less shape needs deploy-time resource
// provisioning, and the CI deploy token (an Account API token) can deploy
// Workers but cannot create KV namespaces: every fixture deploy failed
// Authentication error 10000 on POST /storage/kv/namespaces while
// continue-on-error kept the job green (observed in the 2026-09-22T19:27Z
// deploy run — 0509-fixture-site never existed on the account). The
// 0509-fixture-site-state namespace was provisioned once out-of-band, the same
// fix #4190 shipped for the sibling inbox Worker; pinning its id means a
// deploy only needs Workers write, never KV-namespace write.
//
// The break state has NO TTL and the deploy job never resets it, so it survives
// deploys: a round-trip that forgets to repair leaves the fixture broken while
// every later deploy still reports success. End every round-trip with
// `POST /__break?mode=off`.
//
// The Worker also needs the `FIXTURE_SITE_TOKEN` Worker secret. Without it every
// flip answers 503 and the fixture stays healthy forever, which is why the
// Worker fails loudly rather than reading healthy by default.
{
  "$schema": "../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "0509-fixture-site",
  "main": "./fixture-site.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-16",
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  "kv_namespaces": [
    { "binding": "STATE", "id": "da3bc903dec448d7ae445b7b173723bc" }
  ],
  "routes": [{ "pattern": "fixture.0509.in", "custom_domain": true }]
}
